<title>FRANCE: Strategie Grains revises up EU grain crop forecast.</title>
<headline>Strategie Grains revises up EU grain crop forecast.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>French grain analyst Strategie Grains said on Friday it was revising up its forecast for 1996 European Union (EU) grain production to 202.2 million tonnes from last month's target of 201.4 million.</p>
<p>This would represent a jump of some 15 percent from the 176.5 million tonnes of grain produced in 1995.</p>
<p>In its November report Strategie Grains said the upward revision was mostly in maize, which it now sees at 33.4 million tonnes against 32.9 million last month and 29.5 million produced in 1995.</p>
</text>
